==Strategy==
Marching Kory doesn't have a wave attack like other Kory variants, but his attack power is greatly strengthened and can easily take out spammable units especially on this level. Nevertheless, units that can outrange him will prove rather helpful here as they can consistently chip him down from afar.

Because everything here spawn on a timer, fast units can rush the stage before they intervene, with certain LD units capable of hitting the base behind Marching Kory without having to tear through his health.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] - Almost mandatory for speedrunning, Bahamut can easily cause Marching Kory to flinch on {{1c}} with any Attack Up Combo and stun-lock him. On {{2c}} and {{3c}}, Bahamut needs to deal 157,500/210,000 damage in total from one hit, which is still feasible at level 40 with his Explosion Talent maxed, letting the player easily claim all Timed Score Rewards. On {{4c}}, Bahamut requires support since he cannot hope to deal 315,000 damage before Marching Kory's foreswing finishes.
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]] - Only usually useful from {{4c}}, Mightycat comes from [[Puffer Planet (Merciless)|a difficult advent stage]], but has the invaluable ability to weaken traitless enemies to 50% for 6.67 seconds. Despite having Single Attack and low range, other units can be used to dispose of the Doge Darks and Gabriels so he has a clear shot up close. The Weaken effect allows Bahamut to live longer in the likely event where he is hit, enough for him to actually kill Marching Kory and still have health to spare for the rest of the stage. His Wave Shield ability also comes in handy against Pigeon de Sable, assuming if units with even less range are broght along.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist]] - Being Resistant to Traitless with 100% chance to cause Knockback and a 2-second Freeze, Tourist can tank a hit or two from Marching Kory and utilize its CC effects to artificially create a window of opportunity. It also comes from [[Bombergirl (Deadly)|a very easy advent stage]] and is fairly accessible.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] - A fast LD rusher with decent stats, Courier is a cheap answer to the early-game peons and can quickly kill them with help from meatshields.

